## Context

The existing data/jetp registries contain projects, programme components, repeated financial stages and unresolved observations. Public totals require reviewed identities and an explicit publication boundary, not a sum of ledger rows.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Parent tracker: 0725.

## First test

First failing fixture: a programme and its component share financing, a loan has approval and signature observations, and a missing payment sits beside a true zero. An export must not double-count either overlap, mix stages, or turn the missing payment into zero; each reported amount must resolve to source evidence.

## Actions

Reuse docs/jetp-tracking.md and 0715–0721. Define release schema, identity hierarchy, lifecycle date semantics, strict versus extended attribution, aggregation and currency policies. Audit imported financial-status mappings against source meanings; a register start date is not automatically a signature date. Publish versioned machine-readable exports with coverage, unresolved/conflicting observations and release terms. Keep unavailable payments explicit. Support original and revised pledge perimeters without mixing them.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Release export and dictionary cover four countries with explicit gaps
- [ ] Project/programme/component and multi-tranche rules prevent duplicate totals
- [ ] Event, publication and retrieval dates and date precision remain distinct
- [ ] Totals expose constituent IDs, sources, stages, scope, cutoff and currency rules
- [ ] Versioned downloadable dataset, provenance manifest, validation and reuse/redistribution terms prepared

## Validation

Apply the repository gates for the actual diff. Code work starts with the failing
fixture above; prose/data work records the documentary acceptance check. Preserve
source evidence and report limits rather than manufacturing a successful result.

## Storage implementation contract

Implement the Markdown/CSV publication boundary in `docs/jetp-storage.md`. Validate dossier join IDs and referenced claims; facts remain in the registries. Freeze release inputs before writing a descriptor that references their Git SHA. Public packages must work without the internal DVC remote.

## GitHub planning issue

https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/climate-finance-het/issues/1334

## Progress audit, 14 September 2026

PR #1343 supplies an offline preview, 383 named portfolio identities, 21 unnamed
slots, source-linked country exports and national reported headlines. This is
partial delivery, not a citable release. The scientific fixes in that PR remain
part of 0734 until validated.

Next release work: audit the register-to-financial-status mapping, especially the
South African source-regime category; encode programme/component and tranche
relationships needed for additive aggregates; expose constituent records for any
new total; freeze a release descriptor, dictionary, validation report and reuse
terms. Keep source coverage distinct from implementation. Explicitly decide which
aggregates are defensible and which remain unavailable. Do not treat 301 registered
sources as 301 independent confirmations.

## Audit source replication follow-up

The broader0735audit added `data/jetp/audit-evidence/0735-round2.dvc` with eight
original payloads and a SHA-256 manifest. Its padme push failed on14September2026
(connection refused at127.0.1.1:22). All nine DVCcacheobjects are preserved in the
primary local cache. Before relying on this bundle in a citable remote release,
retry the configured push and verify a clean-cache retrieval/hash comparison.
Do not infer remote availability from the committed pointer. Source publication
terms remain part of this release ticket; the audit did not deploy raw payloads.

The third bilateral audit adds `0735-round3.dvc` and a 33-entry SHA-256
manifest (406,032,031 bytes). Include this separate bundle in the same
remote-replication and clean-cache retrieval acceptance check; retain partial
CSV and duplicate-download annotations. Audit profiles are not a public release.
